IMPORT prelude

-- Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 (Singapore) -- Part 7, wills and inheritance: the saving for a will directing
-- distribution by Muslim law (s 110), the restriction on a Muslim's will (s 111), distribution on intestacy and partial intestacy
-- (s 112), the Mazhab in a probate affidavit (s 113), the Syariah Court's inheritance certificate (s 115), letters of
-- administration on intestacy (s 116), and a married woman's will (s 118).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 2 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/AMLA1966.txt. Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit. The arrangement table at its head is
-- out of step from s 111 onward (it lists "111. Application for probate", "113. Inheritance certificate", "115. [Repealed]");
-- in the body s 111 is the will restriction, s 113 the probate affidavit, s 115 the inheritance certificate and s 117 is repealed.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0282 (Haziq scenario, event h085): a Muslim leaves one third of his estate by will to a
-- registered charity and nothing to any heir beyond the faraid share; is the will valid, and what certificate must the family
-- obtain before the estate is distributed?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the content of Muslim law itself -- the Act states no fraction (no "one third") and no list of heirs or shares; it
-- defers to "the school of Muslim law professed" (s 111(1)) and to "the Muslim law" (ss 112, 115), so the school's limit is an
-- INPUT here, never a constant. Also not encoded: proof of Muslim law from the listed books (s 114); harta sepencarian proportions
-- (s 112(3) leaves them to the court); the Wills Act 1838, Insurance Act 1966 and Probate and Administration Act 1934 themselves;
-- the prescribed fee and the form of application for an inheritance certificate (rules under s 145(2)(e), (f), not retrieved);
-- married women's property beyond s 118 (ss 119 onward); wakaf and nazar (Part 4).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 -- wills and inheritance`

§§ `110 and 111 -- a Muslim's will`

-- s 110: "Nothing in this Act is to be held to prevent any Muslim person directing by his or her will that his or her estate and
-- effects must be distributed according to the Muslim law."
-- s 111(1): "Despite anything in the provisions of the English law or in any other written law, no Muslim domiciled in Singapore
-- may, after 1 July 1968, dispose of his or her property by will except in accordance with the provisions of and subject to the
-- restrictions imposed by the school of Muslim law professed by him or her."
-- s 111(2): "Nothing in this section affects -- (a) the provisions of the Wills Act 1838, other than section 3 thereof; (b) the
-- provisions of the Insurance Act 1966; (c) the provisions of the Probate and Administration Act 1934; or (d) the will of a
-- Muslim dying before 1 July 1968."
DECLARE Testator
    HAS `is a Muslim` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is domiciled in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
        `died before 1 July 1968` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The date test is taken from s 111(2)(d) (the date of death). s 111(1)'s "after 1 July 1968, dispose" could also be read as the
-- date the will was made; the encoding follows (2)(d), which is an inference about how the two fit together.
GIVEN `t` IS A Testator
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 111 restricts the will` IF
    `t`'s `is a Muslim` AND `t`'s `is domiciled in Singapore` AND (NOT `t`'s `died before 1 July 1968`)

-- Whether a gift is within "the provisions of and ... the restrictions imposed by the school" is a question of Muslim law, not of
-- the Act. It is supplied by the caller.
GIVEN `t` IS A Testator, `the school professed permits the disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 111 allows the disposition` IF
    (NOT `s 111 restricts the will` `t`) OR `the school professed permits the disposition`

-- A helper for a school whose restriction is a fraction of the estate. The fraction is NOT in the Act; the caller names it.
GIVEN `share bequeathed` IS A NUMBER, `the limit the school sets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the share is within the school's limit` IF
    NOT (`share bequeathed` GREATER THAN `the limit the school sets`)

DECLARE OtherLaw IS ONE OF
    `the Wills Act 1838 section 3`
    `the Wills Act 1838 other provisions`
    `the Insurance Act 1966`
    `the Probate and Administration Act 1934`
    `English law generally`
    `any other written law`

-- s 111(2)(a) to (c) leave these untouched; s 111(1) overrides "English law or ... any other written law", and (2)(a) carves out
-- section 3 of the Wills Act 1838 from the saving.
GIVEN `law` IS AN OtherLaw
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 111 leaves the law unaffected` IF
    CONSIDER `law`
    WHEN `the Wills Act 1838 section 3` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Wills Act 1838 other provisions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Insurance Act 1966` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Probate and Administration Act 1934` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `English law generally` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other written law` THEN FALSE

§§ `112 -- intestacy and partial intestacy`

-- s 112(1): "In the case of any Muslim person domiciled in Singapore dying intestate, the estate and effects must be distributed
-- according to the Muslim law as modified, where applicable, by Malay custom."
-- (2): "This section applies in cases where a person dies partly intestate as well as in cases where he or she dies wholly
-- intestate."
-- (3): "In the case of a Malay dying intestate, the court may make an order for the division of the harta sepencarian or jointly
-- acquired property in such proportions as to the court seems fit."
GIVEN `t` IS A Testator, `dies wholly intestate` IS A BOOLEAN, `dies partly intestate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 112 sends the undisposed estate by Muslim law` IF
    `t`'s `is a Muslim` AND `t`'s `is domiciled in Singapore` AND (`dies wholly intestate` OR `dies partly intestate`)

-- s 112(3) names "a Malay", not a Muslim, and does not repeat the domicile words of (1). Its application to partial intestacy rests
-- on (2) ("This section applies") -- an inference that (2) reaches (3).
GIVEN `is a Malay` IS A BOOLEAN, `dies wholly intestate` IS A BOOLEAN, `dies partly intestate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may divide harta sepencarian` IF
    `is a Malay` AND (`dies wholly intestate` OR `dies partly intestate`)

§§ `113 -- the Mazhab in the probate affidavit`

-- s 113: "In all applications for probate or letters of administration the affidavit supporting the application must, in the case
-- of a deceased Muslim, state the school of law (Mazhab) which the deceased professed in addition to the particulars required by
-- any other written law."
GIVEN `the deceased was a Muslim` IS A BOOLEAN, `the application is for probate or letters of administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the affidavit must state the Mazhab` IF
    `the deceased was a Muslim` AND `the application is for probate or letters of administration`

§§ `115 -- the inheritance certificate`

-- s 115(1): "If, in the course of any proceedings relating to the administration or distribution of the estate of a deceased person
-- whose estate is to be distributed according to the Muslim law, any court or authority is under the duty of determining the
-- persons entitled to share in such estate or the shares to which such persons are respectively entitled, the Syariah Court may,
-- on a request by the court or authority or on the application of any person claiming to be a beneficiary and on payment of the
-- prescribed fee, certify upon any set of facts found by such court or authority or on any hypothetical set of facts its opinion
-- as to the persons who are ... entitled to share in such estate and as to the shares to which they are respectively entitled."
DECLARE EstateProceeding
    HAS `proceedings on administration or distribution are on foot` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the estate is to be distributed according to Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a court or authority must determine the persons entitled or their shares` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `the court or authority`
    `a person claiming to be a beneficiary`
    `a person not claiming to be a beneficiary`

-- "on payment of the prescribed fee" is read as attaching to both routes (request and application); it could be read as attaching
-- to the beneficiary's application only. The fee amount is in rules (s 145(2)(e)), not the Act.
GIVEN `p` IS AN EstateProceeding, `who asks` IS A Requester, `the prescribed fee is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Syariah Court may certify` IF
        `p`'s `proceedings on administration or distribution are on foot`
    AND `p`'s `the estate is to be distributed according to Muslim law`
    AND `p`'s `a court or authority must determine the persons entitled or their shares`
    AND (`who asks` EQUALS `the court or authority` OR `who asks` EQUALS `a person claiming to be a beneficiary`)
    AND `the prescribed fee is paid`

-- s 115(1) says the Syariah Court "may" certify. No provision in the deposit makes the certificate a condition of distributing an
-- estate, or puts a duty on the family to obtain one. Encoded as a constant so the answer to REQ-0282 can be asserted.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act makes an inheritance certificate a precondition of distribution` IF FALSE

-- s 115(1): the opinion may rest on "any set of facts found by such court or authority or on any hypothetical set of facts".
DECLARE FactBasis IS ONE OF
    `facts found by the court or authority`
    `a hypothetical set of facts`
    `facts the Syariah Court finds itself`

GIVEN `basis` IS A FactBasis
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate may rest on` IF
    `basis` EQUALS `facts found by the court or authority` OR `basis` EQUALS `a hypothetical set of facts`

-- s 115(2): "The Syariah Court may, before certifying its opinion, require to hear the parties on any question of law, but is not to
-- hear evidence or make findings on any question of fact."
DECLARE CertificateStep IS ONE OF
    `hearing the parties on a question of law`
    `hearing evidence`
    `making findings of fact`

GIVEN `step` IS A CertificateStep
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Syariah Court may take the step` IF
    `step` EQUALS `hearing the parties on a question of law`

-- s 115(3): "In any case of special difficulty, the Syariah Court may refer the question to the Legal Committee for its opinion and
-- is, if such opinion be given, to certify in accordance therewith." s 2: "Legal Committee" means the Legal Committee of the Majlis.
DECLARE Opinion IS ONE OF
    `the Syariah Court's own opinion`
    `the Legal Committee's opinion`

GIVEN `referred to the Legal Committee` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Legal Committee gives its opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Opinion
`whose opinion is certified` MEANS
    IF `referred to the Legal Committee` AND `the Legal Committee gives its opinion`
    THEN `the Legal Committee's opinion`
    ELSE `the Syariah Court's own opinion`

§§ `116 -- letters of administration on intestacy`

-- s 116(1): "In granting letters of administration to the estate of a Muslim who dies intestate, the court may if it thinks fit grant
-- letters of administration to any next-of-kin of the Muslim or any other person entitled to a share in the estate under the Muslim
-- law." (2) saves s 18 of the Probate and Administration Act 1934, not encoded.
GIVEN `is next-of-kin` IS A BOOLEAN, `is entitled to a share under Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 116 lets the court grant letters of administration to the person` IF
    `is next-of-kin` OR `is entitled to a share under Muslim law`

§§ `118 -- will of a married woman`

-- s 118: "Subject to section 111, Muslim married women may, with or without the concurrence of their husbands, by will dispose of
-- their own property." The husband's concurrence makes no difference; s 111 still governs.
GIVEN `t` IS A Testator, `the school professed permits the disposition` IS A BOOLEAN, `the husband concurs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a married woman's will of her own property is allowed` IF
    `s 111 allows the disposition` `t` `the school professed permits the disposition`
